  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-11-05T07:13:03.584Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Was experimenting with ways to reproduce the extreme frame drops which VR headsets experience, except on desktop and can reliable reproduce the same frame drops by resizing the desktop window, consistently resizing it leads to having the same frame rate issues VR has with only a 0.365% margin. Leading me to believe that VR headsets are attempting to resize the resolution every single frame.\nfirst photo is the window stationary, second photo is actively resizing the window. this is reproducible with the same results 100% of the time.\nI hope this helps solve the long standing performance issues. <3 -Red",
